oat or int): The height of the triangular face (perpendicular distance from the base to the opposite vertex).\n    length (float or int): The length of the prism (distance between the two triangular faces).\n    \n    Returns:\n    int: The volume of the prism, calculated as (base * height / 2) * length, converted to an integer.\n    """\n    volume = (base * height / 2) * length\n    return int(volume)\n```\n</answer>'
